Allow multiple concurrent AP interfaces on mt7921/mt7925.

The shared mt792x interface-combination table caps NL80211_IFTYPE_AP at 1,
so mac80211's ieee80211_check_combinations() rejects a second AP vif with
-EBUSY before the firmware ever sees it. The mt7925 silicon and firmware
support several BSSes (MT792x_MAX_INTERFACES = 4 is the vif budget), so a
single hardcoded AP limit makes multi-SSID AP mode impossible:

  hostapd: Could not set interface wlan0-1 flags (UP): Device or resource busy

Raise the AP limit to the driver's interface budget in both the default and
the single-channel channel-context combinations.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mt792x_core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mt792x_core.c
@@ -14,6 +14,6 @@ static const struct ieee80211_iface_limit if_limits[] = {
 	},
 	{
-		.max = 1,
+		.max = MT792x_MAX_INTERFACES,
 		.types = BIT(NL80211_IFTYPE_AP)
 	}
 };
@@ -52,8 +52,8 @@ static const struct ieee80211_iface_limit if_limits_chanctx_scc[] = {
 	},
 	{
-		.max = 1,
+		.max = MT792x_MAX_INTERFACES,
 		.types = BIT(NL80211_IFTYPE_AP)
 	},
 	{
 		.max = 1,
 		.types = BIT(NL80211_IFTYPE_P2P_DEVICE)
